{"conjecture": "Long-running systems degrade because each locally correct change incrementally tightens the implicit dependency graph among modules, shrinking the set of future changes that remain locally correct. This tightening is invisible to any single review or test, which only validates the change against the current graph, not against the graph's evolving capacity to accommodate future changes. The system becomes harder to change not because any step was wrong, but because each step optimized for local correctness while permanently consuming global optionality."}
